SPLIT-REALITY PANIC

Duration: 25 seconds
Aspect Ratio: 16:9 cinematic
Tone: Existential sci-fi horror, intrusive, destabilizing
Narrative priority: discomfort > clarity > beauty

🚫 ABSOLUTE LAWS (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
NO STATIC. EVER.
NO HOLDS. NO ESTABLISHING SHOTS.
NO BEAUTY SHOTS.
NO FLOATING OR “SUBTLE DRIFT.”
EVERY SHOT HAS FORCED MOTION + CONSEQUENCE.

Average shot length: 0.6–1.1s
Max shot length: 1.4s
Cuts triggered by audio transients only.

🎥 CAMERA & MOTION LOCKS
Handheld micro-jitter at all times
Real inertia: camera overshoots, corrects, never glides
Uneven zooms, whip-pans, snap reframes
Orbit shots must be imperfect and asymmetrical
Lens occasionally occluded by dust, debris, bodies

🌑 PHYSICS & WORLD RULES
Everything has mass, drag, latency
Dust behaves like heavy regolith, not smoke
Energy displacements push matter outward
Organic matter deforms with delay, never instantly
Jelly entities phase but still displace air and dust
Impacts always affect environment even if targets are unharmed

💡 LIGHTING
Harsh lunar bounce light from ground
Cold rim light from Earth
No soft fills
Hard specular highlights on visors and wet flesh
Sudden exposure spikes during weapon discharge

🔊 AUDIO (STARTS BEFORE VISUAL)
🎵 BGM
Industrial PHONK — ~135 BPM
Distorted 808 bass (sub-heavy, chest-felt)
Metallic percussion (factory impact tones)
Low machine-hum drone
Digital glitch stutters synced to cuts

🎵 First bass hit at 0.3s — before visual clarity

🔊 SFX PALETTE
Sub-bass impacts (felt, not heard)
HUD chirps, clipped error buzz, signal tearing
Wet organic breathing (creature side only)
Bone-scrape groans (low, restrained, NOT roars)
Regolith debris impacts panning across stereo field

📱 SPLIT-SCREEN LAW
Vertical split appears instantly
Asymmetric proportions
Boundary vibrates, tilts, fractures
Split may be violated by entities
Split collapses violently later — never gently

